# atlOS

atlOS is an experimental operating system project designed for educational and research purposes. It aims to provide a minimal, modular, and understandable OS architecture for hobbyists and developers interested in OS development.

## Features
- Minimal kernel with modular components
- Basic process and memory management
- Simple file system support
- Command-line shell interface
- Educational codebase with clear structure

## Getting Started

### Prerequisites
- QEMU or another x86 emulator (**QEMU 6.2.0** recommended)
- **CMake**
- **Cross-compiler toolchain** (x86_64-elf-gcc, GNU ld)

### Cross-Compiler Requirement
**atlOS** requires a cross-compiler for building. The recommended toolchain versions are:
- GNU Binary Utilities(binutils) 2.41
- x86_64-elf-gcc (GCC) 13.2.0
- GNU Make 4.3

### x86\_64 GCC Cross-Compiler Setup 

This section explains how to set up GCC for cross-compiling on Linux.


---

#### 1️⃣ Create working directories

```bash
mkdir -p $HOME/src
mkdir -p $HOME/opt/cross
export PREFIX="$HOME/opt/cross"
export TARGET=x86_64-elf
export PATH="$PREFIX/bin:$PATH"
```

> You may also add these environment variables to `~/.bashrc` or `~/.zshrc`.

---

#### 2️⃣ Install required packages

```bash
sudo apt update
sudo apt install build-essential bison flex libgmp3-dev libmpc-dev libmpfr-dev texinfo wget
```

---

#### 3️⃣ Download, build, and install Binutils

```bash
cd $HOME/src
wget https://ftp.gnu.org/gnu/binutils/binutils-2.41.tar.xz
tar -xf binutils-2.41.tar.xz
mkdir build-binutils
cd build-binutils
../binutils-2.41/configure --target=$TARGET --prefix=$PREFIX --with-sysroot --disable-nls --disable-werror
make -j$(nproc)
make install
```

---

#### 4️⃣ Download GCC sources

```bash
cd $HOME/src
wget https://ftp.gnu.org/gnu/gcc/gcc-13.2.0/gcc-13.2.0.tar.xz
tar -xf gcc-13.2.0.tar.xz
```

---

#### 5️⃣ Create GCC build directory

```bash
mkdir build-gcc
cd build-gcc
```

---

#### 6️⃣ Configure GCC 

```bash
mkdir build-gcc && cd build-gcc
../gcc-13.2.0/configure \
    --target=$TARGET \
    --disable-nls \
    --enable-languages=c,c++ \
    --without-headers  \
    --prefix=$PREFIX 

```

---

#### 7️⃣ Build and install GCC

```bash
make all-gcc -j$(nproc)
make all-target-libgcc CFLAGS_FOR_TARGET='-g -O2 -mcmodel=large -mno-red-zone' -j$(nproc)
make install-gcc
make install-target-libgcc
```

---

#### 8️⃣ Test the installation

```bash
x86_64-elf-gcc --version
x86_64-elf-g++ --version
```
---


For detailed information and installation instructions, see: [OSDev Wiki: GCC Cross-Compiler](https://wiki.osdev.org/GCC_Cross-Compiler)

---

### Building atlOS
You can build and run atlOS on QEMU using the provided script:
```sh
./run.sh clean build-all iso run
```


Or boot from the generated ISO on real hardware (not recommended for production use).

## Project Structure
- `kernel/` - Core kernel source code
- `boot/` - Bootloader and startup code
- `fs/` - File system implementation
- `docs/` - Documentation

